          "title": "You'll want to know: چننا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "چننا — chunnā — \"to choose, to pick\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "چننا (chunnā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from cinoti, \"heaps up, collects\" (CDIAL 4814). CDIAL explains the u as taken from other verbs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
